The Eternal Circuit — licensing

This repository uses two licenses.

1. Creative content: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0)

   Applies to manuscripts, stories, lore, canon and studio documents, artwork
   created for the project, and all other non-code material, unless a file
   or folder says otherwise.

   Full legal text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode
   Summary:         https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

   Attribution: "The Eternal Circuit" by Michael Pass and contributors,
   https://github.com/eternal-circuit/eternal-circuit

2. Software: GNU General Public License v3.0 (see LICENSE-CODE)

   Applies to source code, including studio/experiments/ and the scripts and
   models under studio/research/models/.

Third-party materials keep their own terms and are not covered by either
license. This includes the TempleOS ISO and VM files in studio/archives/.

Notes
- Versions of this repository published before this change were distributed
  under GPLv3, and those grants remain in effect for those versions.
- Under the project's authorship rule (AUTHORSHIP.md), manuscript prose is
  generated by AI models and selected and arranged by a human author. How
  far copyright applies to such material is unsettled and differs by
  jurisdiction. The licenses above apply to the extent that rights exist.
